Job description

Job Responsibilities:


Own the Android SDK end-to-end, including architecture, feature development, bug fixes, version releases, and integration documentation.
Write and maintain unit and integration tests using JUnit and Espresso.
Manage SDK distribution via Maven and Gradle (AAR publishing); own versioning and release scheduling.
Build and improve CI/CD pipelines using Fastlane and GitHub Actions; maintain automation scripts in Python, and Shell.
Debug production issues - memory leaks, crashes, integration failures - using Android Studio Profiler (Memory, CPU, Energy).
Build and maintain sample and demo apps for supply and demand partners.
Implement and maintain support for interactive ad formats (banner, interstitial, rewarded, native, video) following MRAID, VAST, and OpenRTB standards.
Develop and maintain mediation adapters for AdMob / GAM, AppLovin MAX, and IronSource.
Collaborate with backend and data teams on API contracts and feature design.
Support Sales Engineering and partner integrations with technical SDK expertise.

Required skills

7+ years of professional Android development; strong proficiency in Java, solid working knowledge of Kotlin
Deep familiarity with the Android SDK (API 24+): View system, WebView, lifecycle, threading, memory management, and the Android runtime
Experience developing and distributing SDKs as binaries not just app development
Hands-on experience with Gradle build configuration and Maven AAR publishing
Solid test writing with JUnit and Espresso across functional and edge-case scenarios
Proficiency with Fastlane and Ruby or Python scripting for CI automation
Experience profiling and resolving performance issues in Android Studio Profiler
Clear communicator: comfortable with technical documentation, cross-team collaboration, and partner-facing discussions